content.text:
Now I can see the full picture. The Express `req.actor` has `type: "board" | "agent" | "none"` (flat union, not discriminated). I need authz.ts to work with both `RequestCtx` (which has `actor: ActorContext | null`) and Express `Request` (which has the flat `actor` object with all optional fields).

The cleanest structural approach: define a minimal interface in authz.ts that both satisfy:

```ts
interface AuthzActor {
  type: string;
